 "notes": "1956 three-storey office block. Pale blue-grey stucco between white square pilasters with block capitals; two cant bays on the north (viewer's left) half through both upper storeys; single tall windows in the flat bays; a tower bay with a triangular pediment and a round clock face; ground (viewer's left to right): glazed shop, glass lobby door, dark open driveway under the second bay, dark-framed door, grilled openings at the south end. Fractions from the real viewer's left. Cooler blue-grey, charcoal frames, taller stepped pediment with a larger clock, railed storey-3 balcony front under it, glass rooftop rails over the bays, white canopies under the bays, pale open driveway mouth. Cooler/lighter blue-grey #c9d4de; south ground barred gate replaced by blank wall. Pediment rebuilt as 9 fine steps so it reads as a pointed triangular gable over the clock; mirror skipped; large-pane windows, 2 window columns between bay 2 and tower, glass roof rails, pilaster finials already present. Curved balcony not expressible. Bays rebuilt through hyB (one large undivided pane per face, meeting rail pushed to the head, three-tier moulded corbel base, thin cornice). Half-round drum balcony and pediment already addressed / not expressible. Wall nudged to #c9d4de. Clock, roof rails, open driveway, shop window already present; bowed half-round balcony and pilaster banner still not expressible (a swell bay would misrepresent a solid railed balcony). Wall #c9d4de, clock pediment, roof rails, canopy, pilasters, dark shop glass already present. Applied: open driveway mouth darkened #474b51 (a dark lit-from-within drive, not a pale panel). Stacked half-round balcony and navy pilaster banner still not expressible. Tint lift (2026-10-02): wall tints lifted toward the sunlit paint (t' = 1-(1-t)k). Base fix (2026-10-03): cool/grey wallTint = target / painted-stucco base so the warm stucco albedo does not turn it pink.",
